Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 05:41:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] presentation: fast scroller thumb stays grabbed while pressed
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The thumb installed draggable only while alpha was above 0. Alpha snaps to 1
on a scroll, then fades after the visibility delay. A finger held still on the
thumb does not move it and does not emit scrolled, so the thumb faded, the
draggable was removed, and the same pointer fell through onto the content.
Dragging down then scrolled the list up. Pausing mid-drag past the fade did
the same. The hit target was only the 12 dp visual thumb.

Press is tracked with pointerInput until every pointer is up. The down is
consumed in the initial pass so a content click does not also fire; moves are
left for draggable. startDragImmediately skips touch slop, and draggable keeps
consuming moves, so the content scroller yields. The modifier stays installed
while the thumb is visible, pressed, or dragging, including while the list
reports a scroll from the drag itself. Alpha stays at 1 for that whole hold
and, after release, the previous delay-then-fade runs from the start. The hit
rectangle is 32 dp wide, grown toward the content; the drawn thumb stays
12 by 48 dp. systemGestureExclusion covers that rectangle. Hidden and not
held, the thumb has no pointer modifiers.

VerticalFastScroller, VerticalGridFastScroller, and VerticalMasonryFastScroller
share the helper. anikku-harmony VerticalFastScroller.kt Harmony section is
the same pattern and still needs this port.

